  "description": "The best of both worlds: TensorFlow's way of describing a network, PyTorch's way of running it. Deep learning in C#: the layer over the engines that already exist. Describe, train and use a network in C# while the arithmetic runs on .NET's own vector maths out of the box, or on libtorch through TorchSharp when the work gets bigger — swapping between them does not change a line of your model. DeepSharp provides what an engine does not: the model's shape, the path your data takes into it, the training loop, the checkpoints and the charts.",
